# A SPLIT LEVEL (M17 phase 2). A fixture, not content.
#
# The left half of the deck stands three height units above the right half, with
# no ramp between them: you fall off to the right and get back only at the far
# end, where a staircase climbs. That is the "split level" environment type --
# two heights side by side, which the heightfield has always been able to express
# and which nothing has ever used.
#
# It exists to exercise the ADJACENCY THICKNESS RULE. Without it the raised half
# is a slab floating six metres up: you see straight under it, and a body walking
# on the low side walks through empty air where a cliff face should be. The rule
# is untestable without a segment like this, and a segment like this falls
# through without the rule, so they are one piece of work.
#
# The staircase at rows 7-9 climbs one unit at a time, which is SOLO_RISE, so a
# lone player can get back up and the validator's solo flood is satisfied.

name = test_split
base_height = 0
width = 10
length = 10
tags = foot, test, split

